            <ArticleTitle>[Knee pain of rare etiology].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>393-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of chronic knee pain of rare etiology is reported. Conventional radiographs excluded any articular pathology but ultrasound images showed features typical of a transsonic type tumor. Pathologic examination was necessary to establish the diagnosis, the tumor being an Antoni type A schwannoma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
